{
  "name": "l0_keyvalues_lexer",
  "about": "The KeyValues tokenizer FUN_10247280 (0x10247280), driven through its wrapper FUN_101f2f30 (0x101f2f30) over a text until the cursor is NULL, as FUN_101f2360/FUN_101f2180 consume a buffer. The tables FUN_102473e0 (0x102473e0) builds once through FUN_1023eff0 (0x1023eff0) -- A `{}()'` at 0x105794c0, B `{}()':` at 0x105c4ef8 -- and the selector byte DAT_10753641 (.bss, never written) pick table B: the colon is a delimiter. Arms in order: whitespace is every byte <= 0x20 signed (controls, space, bytes >= 0x80); `//` and `/* */` only at token start (`/*/` does not close, `/**/` does, unclosed runs to EOF and returns NULL); a quoted string with `\\\"` as its one escape, newlines kept, EOF leaving the cursor one past the NUL; a one-byte delimiter token; a bare word ending at whitespace or a delimiter, never at `\"` or `/`. Each `kv_token` return states the token, the quoted flag and the next cursor. The NULL-cursor-in arm (out untouched) is not reachable through the wrapper loop and is not asserted; neither is the call after an unterminated quote (retail reads past its buffer). Reported as `fail`, a token, a quote flag, a cursor or the call count differs from retail's.",
